 "# name: ra-rpow-inv-limit-test\n# technique: test a claim no recipe certifies, at instances Sage evaluates exactly or by intervals\n# goal: sage_test KaluzaKlein.RealAnalysis.Sequences.rpow_inv_limit file \"ra-rpow-inv-limit-test.sage\"\n# description: Sage's limit of a^(1/n) is 1\nSEED = 0  # the instances are listed, no sampling\nR = RealIntervalField(128)\ndef B(b):\n    return QQ(1 if bool(b) else 0)\nRI = RealIntervalField(256)\ndef O(values, lhs, rhs, rel='==', edge=False):\n    # symbolic values (π, e, logs, limits Sage computed) are compared by 256-bit intervals; rationals exactly\n    if any(hasattr(v, 'parent') and v.parent() is SR for v in (lhs, rhs)):\n        lhs, rhs = RI(lhs), RI(rhs)\n    return oracle_instance(*values, lhs=lhs, rhs=rhs, relation=rel, edge=edge)\nn = var('n')\ninstances = [O([str(v), '(by norm_num)'], limit(v ** (1 / n), n=oo), QQ(1), edge=(v == 1)) for v in [1, 2, QQ(1) / 3, 100]]\n",
